00:22:41.201 --> 00:22:43.140
They get robbed all the fucking time.

00:22:43.140 --> 00:22:44.226
- Wow.
- I just think

00:22:44.226 --> 00:22:45.540
'cause the infrastructure just isn't there

00:22:45.540 --> 00:22:48.453
and then the next day
delivery that they do do,

00:22:50.087 --> 00:22:53.100
it fucks up the the people who
have to actually deliver it

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:55.650
'cause they have to do these insane routes

00:22:55.650 --> 00:22:56.483
to try and deliver this,

00:22:56.483 --> 00:22:58.280
and they're pissing bottles and shit.

00:22:58.280 --> 00:22:59.227
So a part of me is like,

00:22:59.227 --> 00:23:00.660
"Yeah, I'd love next day delivery."

00:23:00.660 --> 00:23:03.600
But I feel like in America it's not-

00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:04.950
- [Joey] Feasible?
- It's sort of feasible,

00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:07.170
and if you are doing it
something bad is happening

00:23:07.170 --> 00:23:08.003
to someone who is delivering.

00:23:08.003 --> 00:23:10.500
- Yeah, I guess this is
definitely me being privileged.

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:11.333
- It's definitely us being privileged.

00:23:11.333 --> 00:23:12.548
- It's definitely a privileged problem.

00:23:12.548 --> 00:23:13.381
- I sort of talk about it

00:23:13.381 --> 00:23:15.123
'cause it's a complicated thing.

00:23:17.070 --> 00:23:19.365
- There's a bigger underlying
issue to where, you know.

00:23:19.365 --> 00:23:21.090
- Japan, for some reason,

00:23:21.090 --> 00:23:24.210
people don't give a fuck
about being worked like crazy

00:23:24.210 --> 00:23:27.060
for nine hours and being
superficial, I don't know why.

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:28.860
- In the UK, you get next
day delivery as well.

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:30.510
- You do, but in London,

00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:32.460
it seems like it would make way more sense

00:23:32.460 --> 00:23:33.807
to have that work in London.

00:23:33.807 --> 00:23:35.370
But in Wales, you don't have that.

00:23:35.370 --> 00:23:36.210
- Oh you, don't?

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:38.130
- Not really, I lived right next

00:23:38.130 --> 00:23:39.787
to the Amazon warehouse in Swansea

00:23:39.787 --> 00:23:42.660
and it was never next day delivery,

00:23:42.660 --> 00:23:46.293
and I lived next to the
warehouse for the whole area.

00:23:47.790 --> 00:23:49.500
I dunno, London, it makes more sense.

00:23:49.500 --> 00:23:51.000
It's possible, there's a
lot more couriers available.

00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:51.960
- Is there maybe a sense

00:23:51.960 --> 00:23:56.147
of urgency towards fulfilling
customer requests maybe?

00:23:56.147 --> 00:23:58.080
'Cause I assume in Wales,

00:23:58.080 --> 00:24:00.961
not a lot of people are
ordering from Amazon, right?

00:24:00.961 --> 00:24:02.536
- No, there's a lot.
- Surely in Cardiff,

00:24:02.536 --> 00:24:03.742
surely in Cardiff.

00:24:03.742 --> 00:24:04.575
- Maybe in Cardiff there are a lot.

00:24:04.575 --> 00:24:07.065
But I think all the Cardiff
orders are being fulfilled

00:24:07.065 --> 00:24:09.767
by the Swansea because
it's about an hour drive.

00:24:09.767 --> 00:24:11.340
- 'Cause I guess that's what I thought

00:24:11.340 --> 00:24:12.570
where I would understand

00:24:12.570 --> 00:24:14.280
if you lived in the fucking boonies

00:24:14.280 --> 00:24:15.113
in the middle of nowhere,

00:24:15.113 --> 00:24:17.250
Okay, you're not gonna
get next day delivery,

00:24:17.250 --> 00:24:18.660
but if you live in an amazing city-

00:24:18.660 --> 00:24:20.027
- [Joey] This is LA.
- Yeah, this is LA.

00:24:20.027 --> 00:24:23.640
- I mean you can get it,
but it's only certain items

00:24:23.640 --> 00:24:25.050
'cause it's gotta be fulfilled by Amazon,

00:24:25.050 --> 00:24:26.430
which means it's in
their warehouse already

00:24:26.430 --> 00:24:28.737
and they get one of their
couriers to come and get it.

00:24:28.737 --> 00:24:29.970
And that makes more sense.

00:24:29.970 --> 00:24:32.097
But I don't know, the whole
fucking system here is weird.

00:24:32.097 --> 00:24:34.980
And even in Europe, it's
not as good as Japan.

00:24:34.980 --> 00:24:38.940
Japan works, but Japan's had
an amazing shipping network

00:24:38.940 --> 00:24:40.153
for like forever.

00:24:40.153 --> 00:24:42.150
- They've just sort of figured it out.

00:24:42.150 --> 00:24:43.097
- They're so on top of everything,

00:24:43.097 --> 00:24:44.613
that's what they care about.

00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:47.760
- And not a single tip was necessary.

00:24:47.760 --> 00:24:50.467
- Yeah, 'cause people here they're like,

00:24:50.467 --> 00:24:52.740
"Bro, we've got so many issues like guns."

00:24:52.740 --> 00:24:53.718
And then Japan's like,

00:24:53.718 --> 00:24:56.495
"If that fucking package
doesn't fucking turn up

00:24:56.495 --> 00:24:59.280
"when I tell it to, I'm
not voting for you."

00:24:59.280 --> 00:25:00.113
- [Joey] Legit.

00:25:00.113 --> 00:25:01.200
- That's what they give a fuck about.

00:25:01.200 --> 00:25:03.120
- We've only been here a few days

00:25:03.120 --> 00:25:05.730
and within that few days,

00:25:05.730 --> 00:25:09.420
we can feel an entirely
complaining about America.

00:25:09.420 --> 00:25:11.682
- This is just the complaining
about America episode.

00:25:11.682 --> 00:25:12.870
(Garnt laughs)

00:25:12.870 --> 00:25:13.931
- Yeah, yeah.

00:25:13.931 --> 00:25:16.020
- Because it's just this
endless fucking stream.

00:25:16.020 --> 00:25:19.807
- Because America is an endless
loop of dichotomy is like,

00:25:19.807 --> 00:25:21.877
"Okay, oh, this big
company does bad thing,

00:25:21.877 --> 00:25:23.887
"but the reason why it's doing bad thing

00:25:23.887 --> 00:25:25.590
"is 'cause people don't
wanna do anything else."

00:25:25.590 --> 00:25:27.167
And it's just this fucking cycle.

00:25:27.167 --> 00:25:28.890
- 'Cause I get it to a point

00:25:28.890 --> 00:25:32.010
why I've experienced
such bad customer service

00:25:32.010 --> 00:25:35.160
because they have no fucking incentive

00:25:35.160 --> 00:25:36.618
to give a shit about their job.

00:25:36.618 --> 00:25:38.553
And I get it,

00:25:39.690 --> 00:25:41.910
especially dealing with
people with the airport,

00:25:41.910 --> 00:25:44.908
you deal with the most stressed
out people in the world.

00:25:44.908 --> 00:25:47.140
At a level, I get it

00:25:48.720 --> 00:25:50.456
and it's kind of sad in a way,

00:25:50.456 --> 00:25:54.633
where I see a lot of people
in customer service positions

00:25:54.633 --> 00:25:57.960
and it feels like the only
people that you see actually care

00:25:57.960 --> 00:26:01.410
about giving a good service
is when there is an option

00:26:01.410 --> 00:26:03.033
to tip in that occupation.

00:26:04.380 --> 00:26:05.633
- It's true, it is true.

00:26:05.633 --> 00:26:07.503
- I mean, that's just what I've seen.

00:26:08.850 --> 00:26:11.640
There are plenty of customer
service positions in America,

00:26:11.640 --> 00:26:14.640
but only the ones that
tip with my own experience

00:26:14.640 --> 00:26:16.380
is the ones where you really feel

00:26:16.380 --> 00:26:18.333
that they care about the customer.

00:26:21.210 --> 00:26:24.120
Society, right?
- We live in a society.

00:26:24.120 --> 00:26:26.370
- Society.
- I'd love to say that, man,

00:26:26.370 --> 00:26:27.690
dude, I would do different.

00:26:27.690 --> 00:26:29.717
I would totally care.

00:26:29.717 --> 00:26:31.050
I don't think I'd care.

00:26:31.050 --> 00:26:32.220
- No, no, no.

00:26:32.220 --> 00:26:33.870
- I think I'd be like,
"I don't fucking care."

00:26:33.870 --> 00:26:35.010
Why would I?

00:26:35.010 --> 00:26:35.843
It's on my bag.

00:26:35.843 --> 00:26:38.070
- Well, especially if you're
surrounded by that environment.

00:26:38.070 --> 00:26:40.080
It's like, you look like the weirdo

00:26:40.080 --> 00:26:41.430
if you're the one that's caring.

00:26:41.430 --> 00:26:43.620
- I'm sure at LAX, that woman has probably

00:26:43.620 --> 00:26:46.460
had the most horrible
people shouting at her

00:26:46.460 --> 00:26:49.800
and fucking just screaming
and then no repercussions.

00:26:49.800 --> 00:26:50.633
- [Joey] Well yeah, of course.

00:26:50.633 --> 00:26:52.417
- And can fucking walks
off, goes home and is like,

00:26:52.417 --> 00:26:53.280
"Oh, I did nothing wrong."

00:26:53.280 --> 00:26:56.370
- Yeah, I totally get that.

00:26:56.370 --> 00:26:57.203
- It sucks though.

00:26:57.203 --> 00:26:58.036
But it does suck 'cause you're like,

00:26:58.036 --> 00:26:58.869
"Why are you taking it out on me?

00:26:58.869 --> 00:26:59.702
I was nice to you.

00:27:00.717 --> 00:27:03.210
- But it sucks for me 'cause
I happened to be the person

00:27:03.210 --> 00:27:05.730
that all that fucking
frustration got taken out on.

00:27:05.730 --> 00:27:08.430
And it just felt fucking horrible,

00:27:08.430 --> 00:27:10.560
which is not to be given the time of day

00:27:10.560 --> 00:27:13.800
or just to be made to feel
guilty for just trying

00:27:13.800 --> 00:27:15.900
to resolve one issue on my end.

00:27:15.900 --> 00:27:17.750
- Even in the UK, that's pretty rare.

00:27:18.630 --> 00:27:21.420
I feel like there's just
a level of disappointment

00:27:21.420 --> 00:27:23.070
and resentment that everyone has.

00:27:25.092 --> 00:27:26.100
It doesn't really go below that.

00:27:26.100 --> 00:27:29.070
Everyone kind of was
just kinda like, "Yeah."

00:27:29.070 --> 00:27:30.150
- 'Cause I feel like in the UK,

00:27:30.150 --> 00:27:31.087
you can really just like,

00:27:31.087 --> 00:27:33.807
"Look, I'm going through a
fucking bad day right now."

00:27:34.920 --> 00:27:36.758
There's a certain tone

00:27:36.758 --> 00:27:38.460
especially in this kind of situations

00:27:38.460 --> 00:27:40.650
where I feel like it's
much rarer in the UK,

00:27:40.650 --> 00:27:41.483
from what I've seen

00:27:41.483 --> 00:27:43.860
to see people really
have a fucking outburst.

00:27:43.860 --> 00:27:44.693
You know what I mean?

00:27:44.693 --> 00:27:45.637
I mean, that they will.

00:27:45.637 --> 00:27:47.330
- Oh, I've seen plenty, I've seen plenty.

00:27:47.330 --> 00:27:48.570
- It will definitely happen,

00:27:48.570 --> 00:27:53.070
but it's less than what I've
seen here in America at least.

00:27:53.070 --> 00:27:55.170
I just needed to vent a bit

00:27:55.170 --> 00:27:57.930
because I literally
lost about in counting,

00:27:57.930 --> 00:28:00.390
about eight hours of my time to this.

00:28:00.390 --> 00:28:01.890
- I mean like when it's LAX,

00:28:01.890 --> 00:28:04.353
it's triple a mental time.

00:28:05.670 --> 00:28:07.290
You gave eight, but you lost 25.

00:28:07.290 --> 00:28:08.550
- Time moves slow.

00:28:08.550 --> 00:28:10.331
- I feel like I lost a year of my life

00:28:10.331 --> 00:28:12.000
with this experience.

00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:14.310
- I mean, I'd be miserable
if I worked at LAX.

00:28:14.310 --> 00:28:16.560
Fucking worst airport.

00:28:16.560 --> 00:28:17.880
- I'm miserable going through LAX,

00:28:17.880 --> 00:28:18.750
let alone working at it.

00:28:18.750 --> 00:28:19.721
- People were like,

00:28:19.721 --> 00:28:20.554
"Bro, at least we're not in New York."

00:28:20.554 --> 00:28:22.537
I'm like, "You are not fucking any better.

00:28:22.537 --> 00:28:23.497
"What are you on about?

00:28:23.497 --> 00:28:24.427
"You all suck.

00:28:24.427 --> 00:28:26.257
"This is all broken.

00:28:26.257 --> 00:28:28.620
"None of this works!"

00:28:28.620 --> 00:28:31.980
- Yeah, so actually 'cause
we've been to LA before,

00:28:31.980 --> 00:28:33.810
but I think this is the first time

00:28:33.810 --> 00:28:36.432
we've had extended stay in LA.

00:28:36.432 --> 00:28:39.510
- Yeah, the longest time
I've spent in LA in one go

00:28:39.510 --> 00:28:41.315
is maybe five days at most.

00:28:41.315 --> 00:28:43.900
- Yeah, and that's
always been in downtown.

00:28:43.900 --> 00:28:45.570
And every time I talk

00:28:45.570 --> 00:28:49.100
to a local they're
like, "Downtown really?"

00:28:49.100 --> 00:28:51.524
That's the awful fucking sector.

00:28:51.524 --> 00:28:52.357
- It's pretty sketch.

00:28:52.357 --> 00:28:53.203
- Yeah, that's the sketch sector.

00:28:53.203 --> 00:28:55.074
You'll get stabbed or shot

00:28:55.074 --> 00:28:57.000
if you walk down the streets there,

00:28:57.000 --> 00:28:59.190
which is something we've
definitely come close

00:28:59.190 --> 00:29:01.710
to experiencing in
downtown LA around "AX".

00:29:01.710 --> 00:29:03.390
But the reason we normally come to LA

00:29:03.390 --> 00:29:06.536
is because of "AX", and
"AX" is in downtown LA.

00:29:06.536 --> 00:29:10.354
So this is actually our first experience,

00:29:10.354 --> 00:29:12.960
mostly outside of downtown,

00:29:12.960 --> 00:29:15.750
but also getting a chance
to experience others.

00:29:15.750 --> 00:29:17.400
- Actually explore Los Angeles.

00:29:17.400 --> 00:29:20.220
- Yeah, so you guys were
here a few days before me.

00:29:20.220 --> 00:29:22.530
How was your guys' experience so far?

00:29:22.530 --> 00:29:24.480
Well, it was good until I got COVID.

00:29:24.480 --> 00:29:25.350
- That's true, that's true.

00:29:25.350 --> 00:29:29.520
- So I mean, it was good for
the first three or four days

00:29:29.520 --> 00:29:31.170
'cause I was staying in Pasadena,

00:29:31.170 --> 00:29:33.450
which is a relatively nicer part of LA,

00:29:33.450 --> 00:29:35.700
at least everyone in LA
says it's a nice part of LA.

00:29:35.700 --> 00:29:37.016
It was nice to be fair.

00:29:37.016 --> 00:29:40.226
And then you have places like Glendale,

00:29:40.226 --> 00:29:43.017
which is where all the
YouTubers live and stuff.

00:29:43.017 --> 00:29:47.133
And I definitely saw a more relaxed.

00:29:48.300 --> 00:29:49.437
I felt safer

00:29:49.437 --> 00:29:52.860
in Pasadena and Glendale
a million times more

00:29:52.860 --> 00:29:55.080
than in downtown LA, which is not hard

00:29:55.080 --> 00:29:57.423
'cause downtown LA is
just "GTA" in real life.

00:29:59.010 --> 00:30:00.187
I felt a little safer and I was like,

00:30:00.187 --> 00:30:02.647
"Okay, I can actually
kind of walk the streets

00:30:02.647 --> 00:30:04.807
"of Pasadena during the day

00:30:04.807 --> 00:30:06.900
"and it feels just like a regular town."

00:30:06.900 --> 00:30:08.700
It's like kind of nice and
there's like lots of places

00:30:08.700 --> 00:30:11.370
to eat and it's really chill.

00:30:11.370 --> 00:30:13.763
- I just looked like "Drake
and Josh" when I was there.

00:30:14.624 --> 00:30:16.004
I felt like I was on an
episode of "Drake and Josh".

00:30:16.004 --> 00:30:17.253
I don't know why.
- A little bit, yeah.

00:30:17.253 --> 00:30:19.260
I walked past an elementary school

00:30:19.260 --> 00:30:22.050
that looked like it was ripped
straight from "The Simpsons".

00:30:22.050 --> 00:30:23.787
And I was like, "Oh!"

00:30:26.610 --> 00:30:27.963
It was that point where I'm just like,

00:30:27.963 --> 00:30:30.090
"Okay, you know what,
LA might not be as bad."

00:30:30.090 --> 00:30:31.020
And then again,

00:30:31.020 --> 00:30:34.020
there was just those like
just small little instances

00:30:34.020 --> 00:30:35.137
that just made me be like,

00:30:35.137 --> 00:30:39.780
"Mm, yeah, maybe not, maybe not."

00:30:39.780 --> 00:30:42.680
Say, the fucking LAX situation

00:30:42.680 --> 00:30:43.950
or the Amazon situation.

00:30:43.950 --> 00:30:46.680
It's very nitpicking, I know,

00:30:46.680 --> 00:30:47.820
but I think it just goes to show

00:30:47.820 --> 00:30:49.860
how much we've been blessed in Tokyo.

00:30:49.860 --> 00:30:51.520
- I mean, it's nitpicking

00:30:52.740 --> 00:30:54.820
when you choose a place
to live for example,

00:30:54.820 --> 00:30:56.340
visiting and living

00:30:56.340 --> 00:30:58.530
is two totally different experiences

00:30:58.530 --> 00:31:01.050
but it's a lot of little things

00:31:01.050 --> 00:31:02.733
that will build up over time.

00:31:04.140 --> 00:31:07.890
One thing I've really,
really missed is walking.

00:31:07.890 --> 00:31:09.990
I've missed walking a lot

00:31:09.990 --> 00:31:13.560
and I'm sure there are some places in LA,

00:31:13.560 --> 00:31:15.259
which I'm sure you can walk

00:31:15.259 --> 00:31:18.300
but I feel like a lot
of America as a whole

00:31:18.300 --> 00:31:21.150
is just not built for walking at all.

00:31:21.150 --> 00:31:24.240
- 'Cause I remember I was
meeting up with a friend of mine

00:31:24.240 --> 00:31:27.390
and she lives like kind of in the middle

00:31:27.390 --> 00:31:28.650
between Pasadena and Glendale.

00:31:28.650 --> 00:31:33.377
So from my hotel, it was
a 20 minute walk at most.

00:31:33.377 --> 00:31:36.060
And so we were hanging out in Pasadena,

00:31:36.060 --> 00:31:36.960
we had lunch and shit.

00:31:36.960 --> 00:31:37.793
And then I was like,

00:31:37.793 --> 00:31:38.797
"Oh, let's just go back to your place

00:31:38.797 --> 00:31:39.987
"and we'll just hang out."

00:31:39.987 --> 00:31:42.069
And I looked on the map
and it was 20 minutes.

00:31:42.069 --> 00:31:43.013
So I'm like, "Yeah, we can walk that.

00:31:43.013 --> 00:31:45.789
"It's a nice day, fucking
it's the middle of the day.

00:31:45.789 --> 00:31:47.797
"It's what, 2:00 PM in the afternoon.

00:31:47.797 --> 00:31:49.197
"I kinda wanna have a walk."

00:31:50.100 --> 00:31:52.200
She looked at me like
I was a fucking weirdo.

00:31:52.200 --> 00:31:54.007
- She was like, "What are you, homeless?

00:31:54.007 --> 00:31:55.277
"Walking, what the fuck?"

00:31:55.277 --> 00:31:56.547
- And she's like, "We're gonna walk it?"

00:31:56.547 --> 00:31:57.757
And I'm like,

00:31:57.757 --> 00:31:59.647
"Don't fucking look at me like that!

00:31:59.647 --> 00:32:02.257
"Yes, I would like to use my legs

00:32:02.257 --> 00:32:05.940
"'cause I haven't done that
in a while since I got here."

00:32:05.940 --> 00:32:09.667
And she was just like, "Okay."

00:32:09.667 --> 00:32:12.303
And she kind of reluctantly followed me.

00:32:13.290 --> 00:32:15.630
I got five minutes into this walk

00:32:15.630 --> 00:32:17.377
and I turned a corner and I was like,

00:32:17.377 --> 00:32:18.607
"I don't wanna go down that street."

00:32:18.607 --> 00:32:19.882
(all laugh)

00:32:19.882 --> 00:32:20.715
And I was like,

00:32:20.715 --> 00:32:22.820
"Okay, I can see what
you were talking about."

00:32:22.820 --> 00:32:24.600
Yes, it's a 20 minute walk,

00:32:24.600 --> 00:32:28.410
but it's also 20 minutes
of my life potentially

00:32:28.410 --> 00:32:30.903
in a lot of danger at the same time.

00:32:30.903 --> 00:32:33.270
- It's 30 minutes when you
gotta do the Navy Seals checks

00:32:33.270 --> 00:32:34.103
and all of that.

00:32:34.103 --> 00:32:36.580
- Yeah, yeah, when you gotta
dodge all the homeless people.

00:32:40.125 --> 00:32:43.770
I feel weird catching
an Uber to some place

00:32:43.770 --> 00:32:48.356
that's five minutes away,
