"Oh, the first time for you all?

00:43:02.703 --> 00:43:03.840
"All right, yeah."

00:43:03.840 --> 00:43:05.790
So I did the second shot, hated it.

00:43:05.790 --> 00:43:08.320
And then a couple of hours
passed by and I'm like,

00:43:08.320 --> 00:43:10.650
"Okay, Meilyne hasn't called me back yet."

00:43:10.650 --> 00:43:12.720
And so I just when I
thought I was in the clear,

00:43:12.720 --> 00:43:15.400
Meilyne from a distance
fucking scuttles towards me

00:43:16.350 --> 00:43:19.830
and she was just like,
"Tequila shot, Joey?"

00:43:19.830 --> 00:43:23.144
And I just had to go, "Fuck off."

00:43:23.144 --> 00:43:26.257
I literally flipped a
finger and was just like,

00:43:26.257 --> 00:43:29.010
"No, get away from me."

00:43:29.010 --> 00:43:30.559
And I just walked off.

00:43:30.559 --> 00:43:32.165
And Meilyne, she was just like.

00:43:32.165 --> 00:43:32.998
- [Garnt] Fucking ran.

00:43:32.998 --> 00:43:34.049
- Yeah, I literally ran from her

00:43:34.049 --> 00:43:38.610
'cause I knew if I wasn't stern about it,

00:43:38.610 --> 00:43:40.380
she would grab me by the sleeve again

00:43:40.380 --> 00:43:42.540
because I heard from a
bunch of other people

00:43:42.540 --> 00:43:44.657
who were way too nice to
Meilyne that they were like,

00:43:44.657 --> 00:43:46.770
"Yeah, she made me do six shots."

00:43:46.770 --> 00:43:47.603
And I'm like,

00:43:47.603 --> 00:43:49.833
"That's 'cause you have
to say the hard no.

00:43:50.977 --> 00:43:53.506
"It's not just the soft
no, it's the hard no."

00:43:53.506 --> 00:43:55.020
- Pressure, pressure.

00:43:55.020 --> 00:43:56.490
- Did she make you do any shots?

00:43:56.490 --> 00:43:57.600
- I think so.

00:43:57.600 --> 00:44:00.030
I didn't really mind though, one is fine.

00:44:00.030 --> 00:44:01.350
- You only got to do one?

00:44:01.350 --> 00:44:03.240
- I think Meilyne only made me do one.

00:44:03.240 --> 00:44:04.440
- Why did she make me do three?

00:44:04.440 --> 00:44:05.520
- I guess 'cause you were just too close

00:44:05.520 --> 00:44:07.748
to her vicinity wise.

00:44:07.748 --> 00:44:10.230
So I was really worried
'cause you we had food

00:44:10.230 --> 00:44:11.980
and I was like, "This isn't enough.

00:44:12.847 --> 00:44:14.343
"Three courses gone, really?

00:44:14.343 --> 00:44:17.167
"Come on, I'm a six
course kind of guy minimum

00:44:17.167 --> 00:44:19.710
"or at least gimme someone
else's course who didn't finish."

00:44:19.710 --> 00:44:21.729
And then lo and behold,

00:44:21.729 --> 00:44:23.579
people just start bringing out pizza.

00:44:24.721 --> 00:44:25.554
- It was all you can eat pizza.

00:44:25.554 --> 00:44:28.770
- It was all we can eat
like stone bake pizza.

00:44:28.770 --> 00:44:31.323
- Yeah, I think I had
like four whole pizzas.

00:44:32.910 --> 00:44:34.741
- I had a worrying amount of pizza.

00:44:34.741 --> 00:44:38.640
- It was more pizza than any
doctor would ever recommend.

00:44:38.640 --> 00:44:41.850
Even if you were carb
loading for a desert survival

00:44:41.850 --> 00:44:45.630
for 10 weeks, you wouldn't
eat this many calories.

00:44:45.630 --> 00:44:47.497
I dunno, every time they
brought it to me, I was like,

00:44:47.497 --> 00:44:48.330
"Well, I can't say no.

00:44:48.330 --> 00:44:49.897
"I mean, it's a different topping.

00:44:49.897 --> 00:44:51.067
"I gotta try it."

00:44:51.067 --> 00:44:53.811
- That was me with the espresso martinis.

00:44:53.811 --> 00:44:55.750
I think I had five
espresso martinis that day

00:44:55.750 --> 00:44:57.630
and I'm like, "Oh that's why I'm shaking."

00:44:57.630 --> 00:44:59.280
- Yeah, so we had a station

00:44:59.280 --> 00:45:01.770
to give out free espresso
martinis to everyone.

00:45:01.770 --> 00:45:03.086
- Wow.
- [Joey] Wow.

00:45:03.086 --> 00:45:05.280
- I mean, we wanted everyone
to have a good time.

00:45:05.280 --> 00:45:06.780
- No wonder that tab was high.

00:45:07.690 --> 00:45:08.910
- But that wasn't even on the tab.

00:45:08.910 --> 00:45:09.743
- Oh my God.

00:45:09.743 --> 00:45:11.670
- That was a pre-package that we paid for.

00:45:11.670 --> 00:45:13.715
- Yeah, 'cause I remember,

00:45:13.715 --> 00:45:16.470
I went up to the bar after
my first espresso martini

00:45:16.470 --> 00:45:17.951
that they brought out for everyone

00:45:17.951 --> 00:45:20.580
and I was like, "Oh, can I
get another espresso martini?"

00:45:20.580 --> 00:45:22.620
And the dude literally
just points to the side

00:45:22.620 --> 00:45:25.710
because there's literally
this three layered shelf

00:45:25.710 --> 00:45:27.024
of espresso martinis.

00:45:27.024 --> 00:45:28.360
There was 12 espresso martinis.

00:45:28.360 --> 00:45:30.480
And I was like, "Take your pick."

00:45:30.480 --> 00:45:33.600
And I was like, "Oh
shit, all right, cool."

00:45:33.600 --> 00:45:36.540
I just drank three of them and
I was just fucking shaking.

00:45:36.540 --> 00:45:39.590
- So I guess to go to the
start of my experience

00:45:39.590 --> 00:45:40.423
of the wedding

00:45:40.423 --> 00:45:42.480
'cause obviously you
guys' experience was very,

00:45:42.480 --> 00:45:43.730
very different from mine.

00:45:44.640 --> 00:45:47.400
So we had about,

00:45:47.400 --> 00:45:49.530
I think it was only 62
people at this wedding.

00:45:49.530 --> 00:45:50.920
So it was a fairly small wedding,

00:45:50.920 --> 00:45:53.400
but I really, really liked
the size of the wedding

00:45:53.400 --> 00:45:55.110
'cause it was a good amount of size.

00:45:55.110 --> 00:45:57.060
I could keep up with pretty much everyone.

00:45:57.060 --> 00:45:57.893
- You could interact with everyone.

00:45:57.893 --> 00:45:58.726
- I could talk with everyone

00:45:58.726 --> 00:46:00.720
and not feel like it was just
like a convention experience

00:46:00.720 --> 00:46:03.027
where I was having one sentence
conversations with people,

00:46:03.027 --> 00:46:05.340
but have proper, meaningful conversations,

00:46:05.340 --> 00:46:09.330
which is good 'cause I just
wanted to share the good vibes

00:46:09.330 --> 00:46:11.130
and everything like that.

00:46:11.130 --> 00:46:13.350
But I remember like the
night before the wedding,

00:46:13.350 --> 00:46:17.737
I was so fucking, I
dunno what the right word

00:46:17.737 --> 00:46:19.200
to describe it was.

00:46:19.200 --> 00:46:22.410
It was a mixture of nervous and excited

00:46:22.410 --> 00:46:25.110
'cause it was not the bad kind of nervous.

00:46:25.110 --> 00:46:27.082
The way I described it,

00:46:27.082 --> 00:46:28.890
it kind of felt like you were 10 years old

00:46:28.890 --> 00:46:30.360
and it was the day before Christmas.

00:46:30.360 --> 00:46:33.540
And you knew, you knew you were getting

00:46:33.540 --> 00:46:35.400
that N64 for Christmas.

00:46:35.400 --> 00:46:37.800
You knew, that this was
the special Christmas,

00:46:37.800 --> 00:46:40.530
where you were getting
the fucking game console.

00:46:40.530 --> 00:46:44.940
And so I got two hours of
sleep before my wedding,

00:46:44.940 --> 00:46:45.874
before the day of my wedding

00:46:45.874 --> 00:46:48.900
'cause I tried to go to
sleep at a reasonable time.

00:46:48.900 --> 00:46:51.087
So I was gonna go to sleep at around 11.

00:46:51.087 --> 00:46:53.617
And I'm like, "Great, I'm
gonna have a reasonable amount

00:46:53.617 --> 00:46:56.040
"of sleep before my wedding
and can be well rested."

00:46:56.040 --> 00:46:57.444
And then like an hour passes,

00:46:57.444 --> 00:47:00.697
two hour passes and I'm
like, "I cannot get to sleep.

00:47:00.697 --> 00:47:03.367
"Okay, okay, if I go to sleep now,

00:47:03.367 --> 00:47:07.380
"I'll get six hours of sleep now, now."

00:47:07.380 --> 00:47:08.550
An hour passes, all right.

00:47:08.550 --> 00:47:10.770
Five hours of sleep, now, now.

00:47:11.688 --> 00:47:12.521
- That's how it always works.

00:47:12.521 --> 00:47:13.354
- And I was just like,

00:47:13.354 --> 00:47:15.067
"If I just go to sleep now,

00:47:15.067 --> 00:47:17.497
"I'll wake up and I'm gonna have a wife.

00:47:17.497 --> 00:47:18.720
"It's gonna be great."

00:47:18.720 --> 00:47:21.420
And then it gets to about
four or five in the morning.

00:47:24.690 --> 00:47:26.027
I'm in pure copium right now

00:47:26.027 --> 00:47:26.860
'cause I'm just like,

00:47:26.860 --> 00:47:29.467
"What if I just have no
sleep before my wedding?

00:47:29.467 --> 00:47:30.391
"I can function.

00:47:30.391 --> 00:47:32.257
"If I just stay up or not, I can function,

00:47:32.257 --> 00:47:33.997
"that's something I can do before one

00:47:33.997 --> 00:47:35.857
"of the most important days of my life.

00:47:35.857 --> 00:47:36.690
"I can do that."

00:47:36.690 --> 00:47:40.207
But before I like truly
justify it to myself, I'm like,

00:47:40.207 --> 00:47:42.060
"Okay, let's just try something new."

00:47:42.060 --> 00:47:45.840
So I take off all of my sheets

00:47:45.840 --> 00:47:48.450
and take off all my blankets
and I put them on the floor.

00:47:48.450 --> 00:47:51.127
I'm like, "Let's try
sleeping on the floor,

00:47:51.127 --> 00:47:52.740
"on the hard floor."

00:47:52.740 --> 00:47:54.420
And for some reason,

00:47:54.420 --> 00:47:57.390
I don't know if there's
just these like Asian genes

00:47:57.390 --> 00:48:00.270
or something where it just
felt like I was home again.

00:48:00.270 --> 00:48:02.310
And I just immediately conked out.

00:48:02.310 --> 00:48:03.977
- [Joey] Oh my God.
(Garnt laughs)

00:48:03.977 --> 00:48:05.213
- What the fuck?

00:48:05.213 --> 00:48:06.153
- Yeah, I dunno, I was sleeping.

00:48:06.153 --> 00:48:08.130
- Were you reminded of your monk days,

00:48:08.130 --> 00:48:09.114
sleeping on the temple floor?

00:48:09.114 --> 00:48:10.508
- I don't even know, pretty likely.

00:48:10.508 --> 00:48:11.910
It felt like I was sleeping

00:48:11.910 --> 00:48:13.410
on a fucking futon or something.

00:48:13.410 --> 00:48:15.870
I dunno what it was about
sleeping on the floor,

00:48:15.870 --> 00:48:18.350
but I just immediately
conked out after sleeping

00:48:18.350 --> 00:48:21.090
on a nice comfy bed or something.

00:48:21.090 --> 00:48:25.320
And then yeah, we go to the wedding venue.

00:48:25.320 --> 00:48:29.460
And of course, I was tense nervous.

00:48:29.460 --> 00:48:31.590
It was like the feeling
of before you get in,

00:48:31.590 --> 00:48:33.780
you start a panel where you
go on stage or something.

00:48:33.780 --> 00:48:35.367
It's just like you know
this big thing is coming up,

00:48:35.367 --> 00:48:37.980
but you just gotta wait
around for it to start.

00:48:37.980 --> 00:48:38.813
- [Joey] That's the worst.

00:48:38.813 --> 00:48:43.347
- Yeah, I was so fucking jittery.

00:48:43.347 --> 00:48:44.250
- I know.

00:48:44.250 --> 00:48:45.750
- Yeah, 'cause I talked to Sydney

00:48:45.750 --> 00:48:46.980
if she was nervous for the wedding

00:48:46.980 --> 00:48:51.510
and she was like her nerves
ended the moment she woke up

00:48:51.510 --> 00:48:54.483
because she was so busy
before the wedding started

00:48:54.483 --> 00:48:57.150
because she had to go do her makeup,

00:48:57.150 --> 00:48:59.550
go do her hair and all
the bridesmaids as well.

00:48:59.550 --> 00:49:03.150
So she was at the venue from 9:00 AM.

00:49:03.150 --> 00:49:07.470
And I didn't need to
get there till 12 noon.

00:49:08.580 --> 00:49:09.780
- You had the easy job.

00:49:09.780 --> 00:49:13.736
- Yeah, and so that was just a lot of time

00:49:13.736 --> 00:49:17.160
for just me to be alone
with my own thoughts

00:49:17.160 --> 00:49:19.923
and be really, really fucking nervous.

00:49:21.859 --> 00:49:25.560
And so yeah, I was really
tense, nervous, whatever,

00:49:25.560 --> 00:49:28.060
but luckily, I had my boys with me.

00:49:28.060 --> 00:49:29.580
I had my boys.
- The lads were there.

00:49:29.580 --> 00:49:32.643
- The lads were there, my
hype men were there with me.

00:49:33.978 --> 00:49:38.970
I remember going to the boys.

00:49:38.970 --> 00:49:43.950
So to fully explain neither
of these two were my best men.

00:49:43.950 --> 00:49:45.930
It's okay.
- Heartbreak.

00:49:45.930 --> 00:49:46.910
- I'm sorry guys.

00:49:46.910 --> 00:49:48.600
Only Connor was a groomsman,

00:49:48.600 --> 00:49:52.049
but part of the reason
was it, made me realize

00:49:52.049 --> 00:49:55.020
how long it's been since
I've planned this wedding

00:49:55.020 --> 00:49:58.800
because me and Sydney had
planned the wedding basically

00:49:58.800 --> 00:50:00.300
before we had moved to Japan.

00:50:00.300 --> 00:50:03.270
And every role

00:50:03.270 --> 00:50:06.360
or the entire wedding party
was chosen and everything.

00:50:06.360 --> 00:50:07.510
- Before "Trash Taste".

00:50:09.270 --> 00:50:10.200
- The wedding was going

00:50:10.200 --> 00:50:13.290
to originally be before
"Trash taste" even started.

00:50:13.290 --> 00:50:16.650
So it's fucking insane that
I've grown so much closer

00:50:16.650 --> 00:50:19.230
to these two in these past two years

00:50:19.230 --> 00:50:23.730
where when my wedding
was planned, I knew Joey,

00:50:23.730 --> 00:50:26.700
but we'd hung out only a few times.

00:50:26.700 --> 00:50:29.400
And we'd hung out a lot, but
I was not as close to you

00:50:29.400 --> 00:50:30.233
as I am now.

00:50:33.593 --> 00:50:34.863
It was so weird to have a wedding

00:50:34.863 --> 00:50:36.240
that was planned two years ago,

00:50:36.240 --> 00:50:39.210
where now the dynamic is
totally fucking different

00:50:39.210 --> 00:50:40.173
and everything like that.

00:50:40.173 --> 00:50:42.300
- I was just sitting in
the crowding, like, "Yeah!"

00:50:42.300 --> 00:50:43.530
- So I remember,

00:50:43.530 --> 00:50:46.140
we call everyone in to
the main ceremony hall.

00:50:46.140 --> 00:50:49.613
So everyone starts getting
their seats and I go out

00:50:51.720 --> 00:50:54.787
by myself and I'm like,
"Garnt, you got this,

00:50:54.787 --> 00:50:56.003
"you got this.

00:50:56.003 --> 00:50:59.077
"Garnt, you're gonna do
a no tear wedding run.

00:50:59.077 --> 00:51:01.530
"There's going to be zero
crying at this wedding."

00:51:01.530 --> 00:51:04.983
And I go out to myself just
to give myself a breather.

00:51:07.800 --> 00:51:09.390
Me and Sydney had personal vows.

00:51:09.390 --> 00:51:12.990
So I bring out my personal
vows and I'm rehearsing them

00:51:12.990 --> 00:51:13.823
in my head.

00:51:13.823 --> 00:51:15.097
I'm like, "Okay Garnt, you got this.

00:51:15.097 --> 00:51:17.406
"Zero tears, we're not
gonna cry at this wedding

00:51:17.406 --> 00:51:18.356
"You got this, you got this."

00:51:18.356 --> 00:51:20.310
I read the first sentence

00:51:20.310 --> 00:51:24.967
and I start fucking like
my jaw just starts going.

00:51:24.967 --> 00:51:27.300
(all laugh)

00:51:28.650 --> 00:51:31.147
And I'm like, "Oh no, oh
no, this is a bad sign.

00:51:31.147 --> 00:51:32.640
"This is a bad sign."

00:51:32.640 --> 00:51:37.260
And so while I'm doing
this all of my lads,

00:51:37.260 --> 00:51:39.687
all my groomsmen come out and they see me.

00:51:39.687 --> 00:51:42.558
And I'm like, "Guys, I'm gonna
need some hype around me.

00:51:42.558 --> 00:51:44.820
"I'm gonna need some
fucking hype around me."

00:51:44.820 --> 00:51:48.870
And so this was a moment
where I took a page out

00:51:48.870 --> 00:51:49.773
of Connor's book.

00:51:50.640 --> 00:51:52.470
I literally go full monkey mode

00:51:52.470 --> 00:51:53.880
right outside the ceremony room.

00:51:53.880 --> 00:51:54.870
- It works, dude.
- It works.

00:51:54.870 --> 00:51:57.360
I was like, "You fucking got this!

00:51:58.522 --> 00:51:59.730
"You fucking got this!"

00:51:59.730 --> 00:52:01.620
Not realizing that everyone inside,

00:52:01.620 --> 00:52:04.020
could you hear me just
fucking shouting by the door?

00:52:04.020 --> 00:52:06.480
- I heard you shouting at something,

00:52:06.480 --> 00:52:07.950
but I wasn't too sure.

00:52:07.950 --> 00:52:10.140
I was like, "That's Garnt, right?

00:52:10.140 --> 00:52:12.477
- People who fear the shouting type

00:52:12.477 --> 00:52:13.727
are people who haven't tried it.

00:52:13.727 --> 00:52:15.500
If you try it, it actually works.

00:52:15.500 --> 00:52:17.640
If you fully commit to it, it works.

00:52:17.640 --> 00:52:18.977
- Yeah, I mean, that time,
it really fucking worked

00:52:18.977 --> 00:52:21.371
'cause I had so much adrenaline in my body

00:52:21.371 --> 00:52:26.340
that I needed some way to release it.

00:52:26.340 --> 00:52:28.927
And so I remember getting to
the ceremony room and I'm like,

00:52:28.927 --> 00:52:29.760
"Okay, it's good.

00:52:29.760 --> 00:52:30.777
"The shouting helped."

00:52:31.834 --> 00:52:33.310
I'm reset and the shouting's helped.

00:52:33.310 --> 00:52:36.780
I go to the front, I turn around,

00:52:36.780 --> 00:52:39.153
I look at my mom's face
and just immediately,

00:52:41.730 --> 00:52:43.683
I'm a broken man again.

00:52:48.030 --> 00:52:50.820
My cousin told me this after the ceremony,

00:52:50.820 --> 00:52:51.653
but he's just like,

00:52:51.653 --> 00:52:54.427
"If there's one thing you
definitely should not do

00:52:54.427 --> 00:52:56.377
"when you're standing up there, waiting

00:52:57.345 --> 00:52:58.710
"is look at your mom."

00:52:58.710 --> 00:53:00.240
It's look at your parents.

00:53:00.240 --> 00:53:02.823
- That's true, I can understand that.

00:53:03.840 --> 00:53:06.330
- Oh, it's a feeling I can't describe.

00:53:06.330 --> 00:53:08.457
My dad and my mom were fucking tearing up

00:53:08.457 --> 00:53:10.203
and I rarely see them tear up.

00:53:12.090 --> 00:53:14.580
I dunno, what did my face look like

00:53:14.580 --> 00:53:15.473
when I was waiting up there?

00:53:15.473 --> 00:53:16.530
I gotta know.

00:53:16.530 --> 00:53:19.535
- I can do a reenactment of
exactly what you were like.

00:53:19.535 --> 00:53:23.325
You were like (exhales).

00:53:23.325 --> 00:53:24.924
That's what you looked like.

00:53:24.924 --> 00:53:26.446
- You're close, yeah ,
that's pretty accurate.

00:53:26.446 --> 00:53:28.762
- Every now and then,
you'd turn and be like,

00:53:28.762 --> 00:53:30.695
"Oh yeah, (exhales)."

00:53:30.695 --> 00:53:31.528
(all laugh)

00:53:31.528 --> 00:53:33.510
That's what you looked like right before.

00:53:33.510 --> 00:53:38.100
- 'Cause there was a lovely,
what you call it, quartet?

00:53:38.100 --> 00:53:38.933
- Yeah, quartet.

00:53:38.933 --> 00:53:40.890
- It was lovely, killing
it, playing this music.

00:53:40.890 --> 00:53:42.373
And every time they
were about to you know,

00:53:42.373 --> 00:53:44.674
'cause the song ends.

00:53:44.674 --> 00:53:46.170
They're not doing a medley.

00:53:46.170 --> 00:53:48.150
The song finishes and then
they start the new one.

